// case: generic-union-decl-is-refused
// what: `union Option[T]` parses now -- parseTypeDecl calls parseGenericParams
//      for the union arm, the same call the model, fn and trait parsers already
//      made -- and the checker refuses the declaration, because nothing
//      substitutes `T` at a construction. A variant constructor names the
//      variant, not the union, so there is no literal beside the name to infer
//      an argument from, and the payload type `T` would reach mapTypeToC as a C
//      type name nothing declared. The refusal is what remains of the first of
//      the three pieces `std/quarantine/option.orb.quarantined` names.
// expect-error: 'Option[T]' is a union with a type parameter
union Option[T] {
    Some(T)
    None
}

fn main() -> int {
    return 0
}
